---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ToolIcon from '../components/ToolIcon.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';
import { savings } from '../lib/finance.mjs';
import guides from '../data/learning.json';
import '../styles/home.css';
const example = savings({principal:1000,contribution:200,annualRate:4,years:5});
const more = savings({principal:1000,contribution:250,annualRate:4,years:5});
const money = n => new Intl.NumberFormat('en-AU',{style:'currency',currency:'AUD',maximumFractionDigits:0}).format(n);
const tasks = [
 {number:'01',icon:'wallet',title:'What’s my take-home pay?',text:'Turn your salary into weekly, fortnightly or monthly pay. See tax and super separately.',href:'/calculators/salary/',action:'Calculate my pay',area:'pay'},
 {number:'02',icon:'growth',title:'How could my savings grow?',text:'Start with your balance and regular deposits. See what you put in and what interest adds.',href:'/calculators/compound-interest/',action:'Calculate my savings',area:'savings'},
 {number:'03',icon:'checklist',title:'Will my pay cover my bills?',text:'Put paydays and bills on a 13-week calendar. Find a shortfall before the bill arrives.',href:'/tools/cash-flow/',action:'Plan my paydays',area:'home'},
];
const reading = ['salary-including-super-vs-plus-super','how-compound-interest-works','offset-vs-extra-repayments'].map(slug=>guides.find(g=>g.slug===slug));
---
<Base title={SITE.name} description="Free Australian money tools, without the overwhelm. Calculate take-home pay, see your savings grow and plan bills around payday. Clear examples and linked sources.">
 <div class="home-simple">
  <section class="home-intro hl-wrap" aria-labelledby="home-title">
   <div class="home-intro-copy">
    <p class="home-eyebrow"><span aria-hidden="true"></span>Everyday money, made clearer</p>
    <h1 id="home-title">Less guesswork.<br />More <em>clarity.</em></h1>
    <p class="home-lead">Your pay. Your savings. Your next bill.<br />Simple Australian tools to help you work it out.</p>
    <a class="home-primary" href="#choose">Find my starting point <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    <p class="home-small">Free to use · No account needed · All amounts in AUD</p>
   </div>
   <aside class="home-example" aria-labelledby="example-title">
    <div class="home-example-top"><span>A little, regularly.</span><span class="home-example-tag">Worked example</span></div>
    <h2 id="example-title">$200 a month.<br />A bigger buffer in five years.</h2>
    <div class="home-example-total">{money(example.balance)} <span>illustrative balance</span></div>
    <div class="home-growth" aria-hidden="true">{[19,28,39,51,65,81,100].map(h=><span style={`--bar-height:${h}%`}></span>)}</div>
    <dl class="home-example-breakdown"><div><dt>Your money</dt><dd>{money(example.deposits)}</dd></div><div><dt>Interest added</dt><dd>{money(example.interest)}</dd></div></dl>
    <p>Start with $1,000, add $200 at each month’s end, and assume 4% a year compounded monthly. Before tax, fees and inflation. An example, not a bank offer or forecast.</p>
    <a href="/calculators/compound-interest/">Try your own numbers <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
   </aside>
  </section>
  <section class="home-choose hl-wrap" id="choose" aria-labelledby="choose-title">
   <div class="home-section-heading"><div><p class="home-eyebrow">Start with one question</p><h2 id="choose-title">What would you like to work out?</h2></div><a href="/tools/">See all tools →</a></div>
   <div class="home-task-grid">{tasks.map(task=><a class="home-task" href={task.href} data-money-area={task.area}><div class="home-task-top"><span class="home-task-icon"><ToolIcon name={task.icon}/></span><span>{task.number}</span></div><h3>{task.title}</h3><p>{task.text}</p><span class="home-task-action">{task.action}<span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span></a>)}</div>
   <p class="home-other">Looking at a home loan? <a href="/calculators/mortgage/">Work out repayments &amp; offsets →</a></p>
  </section>
  <section class="home-understand hl-wrap" aria-labelledby="understand-title">
   <div class="home-section-heading"><div><p class="home-eyebrow">Understand, then decide</p><h2 id="understand-title">One idea at a time.</h2></div><a href="/learn/">Explore the guides →</a></div>
   <div class="home-reading">{reading.map((guide,i)=><a href={`/learn/${guide.slug}/`}><span class="home-reading-number">0{i+1}</span><div><small>{guide.category} · {guide.minutes} min</small><h3>{guide.title}</h3><p>{guide.summary}</p></div><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>)}</div>
  </section>
  <section class="home-practice hl-wrap" aria-labelledby="practice-title">
   <div><p class="home-eyebrow">Put the example to work</p><h2 id="practice-title">What changes if you save another $50?</h2><p>Keep the same starting balance, five years and hypothetical 4% rate. Increasing the monthly deposit from $200 to $250 produces {money(more.balance)} instead of {money(example.balance)}.</p><p>That is about {money(more.balance-example.balance)} more. Of that difference, $3,000 comes from the extra deposits; the rest is additional interest. Separating deposits from interest helps you see what you control.</p></div>
   <div class="home-practice-aside"><h3>Try one change at a time.</h3><ol><li>Enter an amount you could save regularly.</li><li>Keep the rate and time fixed; change the deposit.</li><li>Then lower the rate to see a less optimistic scenario.</li></ol><p>Real bank rates can change. The model uses monthly compounding; a bank may calculate daily. <a href="/methodology/">See the assumptions</a>.</p><a href="/learn/how-compound-interest-works/">Understand interest on interest →</a></div>
  </section>
  <section class="home-trust hl-wrap" aria-labelledby="trust-title"><h2 id="trust-title">Useful numbers.<br />Clear limits.</h2><div><p>Howloop is an independent money education project. Our guides connect worked examples with public sources; our tools let you try those examples with your own numbers. We do not accept payment to rank bank products.</p><p>Calculations run in your browser. Optional saved plans stay on your device. These are educational estimates, not personal financial advice, and have not been reviewed by a licensed financial adviser. <a href="/about/#publisher">About the publisher</a> · <a href="/editorial-policy/">How we check our work</a> · <a href="/contact/">Report a correction</a>.</p></div></section>
 </div>
</Base>
